## 2. Backend Checklist (per admin module)

### Routes (`routes/admin.php`)
```php
Route::middleware(['auth', 'admin'])->prefix('admin')->name('admin.')->group(function () {
    // Custom actions BEFORE resource routes
    Route::patch('categories/{category}/reorder', [CategoryController::class, 'reorder'])
        ->name('categories.reorder');

    Route::resource('categories', CategoryController::class)->except(['show']);
});
```

### Controller
```php
class CategoryController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(private readonly CategoryService $categoryService)
    {
        $this->authorizeResource(Category::class, 'category');
    }

    public function index(Request $request): Response { /* ... */ }

    // Non-resource actions need explicit authorize()
    public function reorder(ReorderCategoryRequest $request, Category $category): RedirectResponse
    {
        $this->authorize('update', $category);
        $this->categoryService->reorder(/* validated data */);
        return back()->with('success', '...');
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- Extend `App\Http\Controllers\Controller` (must extend `Illuminate\Routing\Controller` for `authorizeResource` / `middleware()`).
- Inject services via constructor — never put business logic in the controller.
- Return typed responses: `Response` (Inertia) or `RedirectResponse`.
- Use `$request->validated()` — never `$request->all()`.
- Pass Inertia props through Resources: `(new CategoryResource($model))->resolve()` or `CategoryResource::collection($paginator)`.

### FormRequest
```php
public function authorize(): bool
{
    return $this->user()->can('create', Category::class);
    // or: $this->user()->can('update', $this->route('category'));
}

public function rules(): array
{
    return $this->categoryRules($this->route('category')?->id);
}
```

- Put cross-field / domain validation in `withValidator()` or the service (e.g. cycle prevention).
- Use `prepareForValidation()` to normalize input (`''` → `null`).

### Policy
```php
public function update(User $user, Category $category): bool
{
    return $user->hasPermission('categories', 'edit');
}
```

- One policy per model; map actions to permission scopes from `config/permissions.php`.
- Never check `role === 'admin'` inline in controllers — use Policy + `hasPermission()`.
- Register via `authorizeResource` for standard CRUD; call `$this->authorize()` for custom routes.

### Service
- One `{Model}Service` per complex domain area.
- Wrap writes in `DB::transaction()` when updating multiple rows.
- Throw `ValidationException::withMessages()` for business-rule failures the user can fix.
- Return plain arrays for Inertia — let Resources shape individual nodes inside the service if needed.

### Model scopes
```php
public function scopeSearch($query, ?string $search)
{
    if (blank($search)) return $query;
    return $query->where(fn ($q) => $q->where('name', 'like', "%{$search}%")
        ->orWhere('slug', 'like', "%{$search}%"));
}
```

- Always no-op when filter is blank.
- Keep scopes on the model; don't duplicate filter logic in controllers.

